	/// Count of unique Transitional Housing chains (continuous tenancy sequences) in service as of the selected date. A chain is a sequence of tenancies where the gap between vacating one property and starting the next is 3 days or less. Counts distinct chains rather than individual tenancies to accurately reflect households served. Use Date Table slicer to view historical snapshots; defaults to current date if no date selected. Caveat: households are approximated by continuous-stay chains keyed on Chain ID + Tangata Whaiora ID + Chain Start Date; ~75% of historical TH tenancies have a blank Tangata Whaiora ID, so the household count is less reliable for the blank-client majority of historical records.
	measure 'TH Households Still in Service' = ```
			VAR _IsDateFiltered = ISFILTERED('Date Table')
			VAR _ReferenceDate = 
			    IF(
			        _IsDateFiltered,
			        MAX('Date Table'[Calendar Date]),
			        TODAY()
			    )
			
			// All TH tenancies
			VAR AllTHTenancies = 
			    CALCULATETABLE(
			        'Tenancy',
			        'Property'[Program] = "Transitional Housing"
			    )
			
			// Group by chain to get chain-level aggregates
			VAR ChainInfo = 
			    GROUPBY(
			        AllTHTenancies,
			        'Tenancy'[Chain ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Tangata Whaiora ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date],
			        "MaxTenancyStart", MAXX(CURRENTGROUP(), 'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date]),
			        "MaxVacatedDate", MAXX(CURRENTGROUP(), 'Tenancy'[Vacated Date]),
			        "HasActiveAtRef", SUMX(
			            CURRENTGROUP(),
			            IF(
			                'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date] <= _ReferenceDate &&
			                (ISBLANK('Tenancy'[Vacated Date]) || 'Tenancy'[Vacated Date] > _ReferenceDate),
			                1, 0
			            )
			        )
			    )
			
			// Filter to chains that were IN SERVICE at the reference date:
			// - Chain started on or before reference date AND
			// - Chain was active (not yet vacated or vacated after reference date)
			VAR FilteredChains = 
			    FILTER(
			        ChainInfo,
			        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date] <= _ReferenceDate &&
			        (
			            [HasActiveAtRef] > 0 ||
			            ISBLANK([MaxVacatedDate]) ||
			            [MaxVacatedDate] > _ReferenceDate
			        )
			    )
			
			RETURN
			    COUNTROWS(FilteredChains)
			```
		formatString: #,0
		displayFolder: 09. THVM Dashboard\Length of Stay
		lineageTag: 12bdfc32-3159-4fb2-96a9-be6c1ae2311a

	/// Percentage of Transitional Housing chains in service as of the selected date with short stay (0-12 weeks from Chain Start Date). Uses chain-based calculation where a chain is a sequence of tenancies with gaps of 3 days or less. Short stay indicates households recently entering the program. Use Date Table slicer to view historical snapshots; defaults to current date if no date selected. Caveat: chains are keyed on Chain ID + Tangata Whaiora ID + Chain Start Date; ~75% of historical TH tenancies have a blank Tangata Whaiora ID, so chain grouping - and this percentage - is less reliable for the blank-client majority of historical records.
	measure 'TH In Service - Short Stay %' = ```
			VAR _IsDateFiltered = ISFILTERED('Date Table')
			VAR _ReferenceDate = 
			    IF(
			        _IsDateFiltered,
			        MAX('Date Table'[Calendar Date]),
			        TODAY()
			    )
			
			// All TH tenancies
			VAR AllTHTenancies = 
			    CALCULATETABLE(
			        'Tenancy',
			        'Property'[Program] = "Transitional Housing"
			    )
			
			// Group by chain to get chain-level aggregates
			VAR ChainInfo = 
			    GROUPBY(
			        AllTHTenancies,
			        'Tenancy'[Chain ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Tangata Whaiora ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date],
			        "MaxTenancyStart", MAXX(CURRENTGROUP(), 'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date]),
			        "MaxVacatedDate", MAXX(CURRENTGROUP(), 'Tenancy'[Vacated Date]),
			        "HasActiveAtRef", SUMX(
			            CURRENTGROUP(),
			            IF(
			                'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date] <= _ReferenceDate &&
			                (ISBLANK('Tenancy'[Vacated Date]) || 'Tenancy'[Vacated Date] > _ReferenceDate),
			                1, 0
			            )
			        )
			    )
			
			// Filter to chains that were IN SERVICE at the reference date
			VAR FilteredChains = 
			    FILTER(
			        ChainInfo,
			        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date] <= _ReferenceDate &&
			        (
			            [HasActiveAtRef] > 0 ||
			            ISBLANK([MaxVacatedDate]) ||
			            [MaxVacatedDate] > _ReferenceDate
			        )
			    )
			
			// Add stay weeks calculation
			VAR ChainsWithStay = 
			    ADDCOLUMNS(
			        FilteredChains,
			        "StayWeeks", DATEDIFF('Tenancy'[Chain Start Date], _ReferenceDate, WEEK)
			    )
			
			VAR TotalCount = COUNTROWS(ChainsWithStay)
			VAR ShortStayCount = COUNTROWS(FILTER(ChainsWithStay, [StayWeeks] <= 12))
			
			RETURN
			    DIVIDE(ShortStayCount, TotalCount, BLANK())
			```
		formatString: 0.0%
		displayFolder: 09. THVM Dashboard\Length of Stay
		lineageTag: fbc5f129-8259-4f31-b567-5c35d8460913

	/// Percentage of Transitional Housing chains in service as of the selected date with medium stay (over 12 and up to 52 weeks from Chain Start Date; chains of exactly 12 weeks fall in Short Stay). Uses chain-based calculation where a chain is a sequence of tenancies with gaps of 3 days or less. Medium stay represents households within the standard transitional housing timeframe. Use Date Table slicer to view historical snapshots; defaults to current date if no date selected. Caveat: chains are keyed on Chain ID + Tangata Whaiora ID + Chain Start Date; ~75% of historical TH tenancies have a blank Tangata Whaiora ID, so chain grouping - and this percentage - is less reliable for the blank-client majority of historical records.
	measure 'TH In Service - Medium Stay %' = ```
			VAR _IsDateFiltered = ISFILTERED('Date Table')
			VAR _ReferenceDate = 
			    IF(
			        _IsDateFiltered,
			        MAX('Date Table'[Calendar Date]),
			        TODAY()
			    )
			
			// All TH tenancies
			VAR AllTHTenancies = 
			    CALCULATETABLE(
			        'Tenancy',
			        'Property'[Program] = "Transitional Housing"
			    )
			
			// Group by chain to get chain-level aggregates
			VAR ChainInfo = 
			    GROUPBY(
			        AllTHTenancies,
			        'Tenancy'[Chain ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Tangata Whaiora ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date],
			        "MaxTenancyStart", MAXX(CURRENTGROUP(), 'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date]),
			        "MaxVacatedDate", MAXX(CURRENTGROUP(), 'Tenancy'[Vacated Date]),
			        "HasActiveAtRef", SUMX(
			            CURRENTGROUP(),
			            IF(
			                'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date] <= _ReferenceDate &&
			                (ISBLANK('Tenancy'[Vacated Date]) || 'Tenancy'[Vacated Date] > _ReferenceDate),
			                1, 0
			            )
			        )
			    )
			
			// Filter to chains that were IN SERVICE at the reference date
			VAR FilteredChains = 
			    FILTER(
			        ChainInfo,
			        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date] <= _ReferenceDate &&
			        (
			            [HasActiveAtRef] > 0 ||
			            ISBLANK([MaxVacatedDate]) ||
			            [MaxVacatedDate] > _ReferenceDate
			        )
			    )
			
			// Add stay weeks calculation
			VAR ChainsWithStay = 
			    ADDCOLUMNS(
			        FilteredChains,
			        "StayWeeks", DATEDIFF('Tenancy'[Chain Start Date], _ReferenceDate, WEEK)
			    )
			
			VAR TotalCount = COUNTROWS(ChainsWithStay)
			VAR MediumStayCount = COUNTROWS(FILTER(ChainsWithStay, [StayWeeks] > 12 && [StayWeeks] <= 52))
			
			RETURN
			    DIVIDE(MediumStayCount, TotalCount, BLANK())
			```
		formatString: 0.0%
		displayFolder: 09. THVM Dashboard\Length of Stay
		lineageTag: 09f72061-815a-4a1e-86e4-19c6078625dc

	/// Percentage of Transitional Housing chains in service as of the selected date with long stay (52-104 weeks from Chain Start Date). Uses chain-based calculation where a chain is a sequence of tenancies with gaps of 3 days or less. Long stay indicates households exceeding standard transitional timeframe. Use Date Table slicer to view historical snapshots; defaults to current date if no date selected. Caveat: chains are keyed on Chain ID + Tangata Whaiora ID + Chain Start Date; ~75% of historical TH tenancies have a blank Tangata Whaiora ID, so chain grouping - and this percentage - is less reliable for the blank-client majority of historical records.
	measure 'TH In Service - Long Stay %' = ```
			VAR _IsDateFiltered = ISFILTERED('Date Table')
			VAR _ReferenceDate = 
			    IF(
			        _IsDateFiltered,
			        MAX('Date Table'[Calendar Date]),
			        TODAY()
			    )
			
			// All TH tenancies
			VAR AllTHTenancies = 
			    CALCULATETABLE(
			        'Tenancy',
			        'Property'[Program] = "Transitional Housing"
			    )
			
			// Group by chain to get chain-level aggregates
			VAR ChainInfo = 
			    GROUPBY(
			        AllTHTenancies,
			        'Tenancy'[Chain ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Tangata Whaiora ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date],
			        "MaxTenancyStart", MAXX(CURRENTGROUP(), 'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date]),
			        "MaxVacatedDate", MAXX(CURRENTGROUP(), 'Tenancy'[Vacated Date]),
			        "HasActiveAtRef", SUMX(
			            CURRENTGROUP(),
			            IF(
			                'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date] <= _ReferenceDate &&
			                (ISBLANK('Tenancy'[Vacated Date]) || 'Tenancy'[Vacated Date] > _ReferenceDate),
			                1, 0
			            )
			        )
			    )
			
			// Filter to chains that were IN SERVICE at the reference date
			VAR FilteredChains = 
			    FILTER(
			        ChainInfo,
			        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date] <= _ReferenceDate &&
			        (
			            [HasActiveAtRef] > 0 ||
			            ISBLANK([MaxVacatedDate]) ||
			            [MaxVacatedDate] > _ReferenceDate
			        )
			    )
			
			// Add stay weeks calculation
			VAR ChainsWithStay = 
			    ADDCOLUMNS(
			        FilteredChains,
			        "StayWeeks", DATEDIFF('Tenancy'[Chain Start Date], _ReferenceDate, WEEK)
			    )
			
			VAR TotalCount = COUNTROWS(ChainsWithStay)
			VAR LongStayCount = COUNTROWS(FILTER(ChainsWithStay, [StayWeeks] > 52 && [StayWeeks] <= 104))
			
			RETURN
			    DIVIDE(LongStayCount, TotalCount, BLANK())
			```
		formatString: 0.0%
		displayFolder: 09. THVM Dashboard\Length of Stay
		lineageTag: 270a825c-8058-43fa-998e-c649799206d7

	/// Percentage of Transitional Housing chains in service as of the selected date with ultra-long stay (>104 weeks from Chain Start Date). Uses chain-based calculation where a chain is a sequence of tenancies with gaps of 3 days or less. Ultra-long stay indicates households significantly exceeding transitional housing intent, priority for permanent housing. Use Date Table slicer to view historical snapshots; defaults to current date if no date selected. Caveat: ~75% of historical TH tenancies have a blank Tangata Whaiora ID; for those clients the chain is identified by Chain ID + Chain Start Date alone (Chain ID is unique only within a client), so historical chain figures may over- or under-merge and should be treated as indicative rather than exact.
	measure 'TH In Service - Ultra-Long Stay %' = ```
			VAR _IsDateFiltered = ISFILTERED('Date Table')
			VAR _ReferenceDate = 
			    IF(
			        _IsDateFiltered,
			        MAX('Date Table'[Calendar Date]),
			        TODAY()
			    )
			
			// All TH tenancies
			VAR AllTHTenancies = 
			    CALCULATETABLE(
			        'Tenancy',
			        'Property'[Program] = "Transitional Housing"
			    )
			
			// Group by chain to get chain-level aggregates
			VAR ChainInfo = 
			    GROUPBY(
			        AllTHTenancies,
			        'Tenancy'[Chain ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Tangata Whaiora ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date],
			        "MaxTenancyStart", MAXX(CURRENTGROUP(), 'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date]),
			        "MaxVacatedDate", MAXX(CURRENTGROUP(), 'Tenancy'[Vacated Date]),
			        "HasActiveAtRef", SUMX(
			            CURRENTGROUP(),
			            IF(
			                'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date] <= _ReferenceDate &&
			                (ISBLANK('Tenancy'[Vacated Date]) || 'Tenancy'[Vacated Date] > _ReferenceDate),
			                1, 0
			            )
			        )
			    )
			
			// Filter to chains that were IN SERVICE at the reference date
			VAR FilteredChains = 
			    FILTER(
			        ChainInfo,
			        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date] <= _ReferenceDate &&
			        (
			            [HasActiveAtRef] > 0 ||
			            ISBLANK([MaxVacatedDate]) ||
			            [MaxVacatedDate] > _ReferenceDate
			        )
			    )
			
			// Add stay weeks calculation
			VAR ChainsWithStay = 
			    ADDCOLUMNS(
			        FilteredChains,
			        "StayWeeks", DATEDIFF('Tenancy'[Chain Start Date], _ReferenceDate, WEEK)
			    )
			
			VAR TotalCount = COUNTROWS(ChainsWithStay)
			VAR UltraLongStayCount = COUNTROWS(FILTER(ChainsWithStay, [StayWeeks] > 104))
			
			RETURN
			    DIVIDE(UltraLongStayCount, TotalCount, BLANK())
			```
		formatString: 0.0%
		displayFolder: 09. THVM Dashboard\Length of Stay
		lineageTag: 9515142b-f0d4-4501-857b-28d140f03c79

	/// Median exit time in weeks for TH chains that exited in the 12 months ending at the selected date, filtered by stay category. Uses chain-based calculation (Chain Start Date to final Vacated Date) where a chain is a sequence of tenancies with gaps of 3 days or less. Use 'Stay Category' slicer: Short (0-12 wks), Medium (12-52 wks), Long (52-104 wks), Ultra-Long (>104 wks). Excludes internal transfers. Use Date Table slicer to view historical periods; defaults to current date if no date selected. Caveat: chains are identified by Chain ID + Tangata Whaiora ID + Chain Start Date; roughly 75% of historical TH tenancies have a blank Tangata Whaiora ID, so chain grouping - and this metric - is less reliable for the blank-client majority of historical records.
	measure 'TH Median Exit Time by Stay (Weeks)' = ```
			VAR _IsDateFiltered = ISFILTERED('Date Table')
			VAR _ReferenceDate = 
			    IF(
			        _IsDateFiltered,
			        MAX('Date Table'[Calendar Date]),
			        TODAY()
			    )
			VAR _StartDate = EOMONTH(_ReferenceDate, -12) + 1
			VAR _EndDate = EOMONTH(_ReferenceDate, 0)
			
			// All TH tenancies
			VAR AllTHTenancies = 
			    CALCULATETABLE(
			        'Tenancy',
			        'Property'[Program] = "Transitional Housing"
			    )
			
			// Get chain-level summary
			VAR ChainInfo =
			    GROUPBY(
			        AllTHTenancies,
			        'Tenancy'[Chain ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Tangata Whaiora ID],
			        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date],
			        "MaxTenancyStart", MAXX(CURRENTGROUP(), 'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date])
			    )
			
			// FIX: exit = the LAST tenancy's Vacated Date (blank => still in service), not MAX(Vacated) across the chain
			VAR ChainWithLastReason =
			    ADDCOLUMNS(
			        ChainInfo,
			        "ChainExitDate",
			        VAR _ChainID = 'Tenancy'[Chain ID]
			        VAR _TangataID = 'Tenancy'[Tangata Whaiora ID]
			        VAR _ChainStart = 'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date]
			        VAR _MaxStart = [MaxTenancyStart]
			        RETURN
			            MAXX(
			                FILTER(
			                    AllTHTenancies,
			                    'Tenancy'[Chain ID] = _ChainID &&
			                    'Tenancy'[Tangata Whaiora ID] = _TangataID &&
			                    'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date] = _ChainStart &&
			                    'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date] = _MaxStart
			                ),
			                'Tenancy'[Vacated Date]
			            ),
			        // Tenancies sharing the last start date: the highest Leaving Reason, then Exit Point, sets the outcome
			        "LastExitOutcome",
			        VAR _ChainID = 'Tenancy'[Chain ID]
			        VAR _TangataID = 'Tenancy'[Tangata Whaiora ID]
			        VAR _ChainStart = 'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date]
			        VAR _MaxStart = [MaxTenancyStart]
			        RETURN
			            MAXX(
			                TOPN(
			                    1,
			                    FILTER(
			                        AllTHTenancies,
			                        'Tenancy'[Chain ID] = _ChainID &&
			                        'Tenancy'[Tangata Whaiora ID] = _TangataID &&
			                        'Tenancy'[Chain Start Date] = _ChainStart &&
			                        'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date] = _MaxStart
			                    ),
			                    'Tenancy'[Leaving Reason], DESC,
			                    'Tenancy'[Exit Point], DESC
			                ),
			                'Tenancy'[Exit Outcome]
			            )
			    )
			
			// Filter to chains that exited in 12-month window (excluding internal transfers)
			VAR ExitedChains = 
			    FILTER(
			        ChainWithLastReason,
			        NOT ISBLANK([ChainExitDate]) &&
			        [ChainExitDate] >= _StartDate &&
			        [ChainExitDate] <= _EndDate &&
			        NOT([LastExitOutcome] = "Internal Transfer")
			    )
			
			// Add stay weeks calculation
			VAR ExitedWithWeeks = 
			    ADDCOLUMNS(
			        ExitedChains,
			        "StayWeeks", DATEDIFF('Tenancy'[Chain Start Date], [ChainExitDate], WEEK)
			    )
			
			VAR SelectedCategory = SELECTEDVALUE('Stay Category'[Category], "All")
			
			RETURN
			    SWITCH(
			        SelectedCategory,
			        "Short", MEDIANX(FILTER(ExitedWithWeeks, [StayWeeks] <= 12), [StayWeeks]),
			        "Medium", MEDIANX(FILTER(ExitedWithWeeks, [StayWeeks] > 12 && [StayWeeks] <= 52), [StayWeeks]),
			        "Long", MEDIANX(FILTER(ExitedWithWeeks, [StayWeeks] > 52 && [StayWeeks] <= 104), [StayWeeks]),
			        "Ultra-Long", MEDIANX(FILTER(ExitedWithWeeks, [StayWeeks] > 104), [StayWeeks]),
			        MEDIANX(ExitedWithWeeks, [StayWeeks])
			    )
			```
		formatString: #,0.0
		displayFolder: 09. THVM Dashboard\Length of Stay
		lineageTag: a5d4981b-dee8-4aa5-847a-f088ea4f26a9

	/// Monthly exit rate calculated as (Exits in month / Households serviced in month). Shows the proportion of households that exited during the selected month. Excludes internal transfers. Per HUD THVM Dashboard specifications. Use Date Table slicer to view historical months; defaults to current month if no date selected.
	measure 'TH Exit Rate % (Current)' =
			VAR _IsDateFiltered = ISFILTERED('Date Table')
			VAR _ReferenceDate =
			    IF(
			        _IsDateFiltered,
			        MAX('Date Table'[Calendar Date]),
			        TODAY()
			    )
			VAR _MonthStart = EOMONTH(_ReferenceDate, -1) + 1
			VAR _MonthEnd = EOMONTH(_ReferenceDate, 0)
			VAR _ExitsThisMonth =
			    COUNTROWS(
			        FILTER(
			            'Tenancy',
			            'Tenancy'[Vacated Date] >= _MonthStart &&
			            'Tenancy'[Vacated Date] <= _MonthEnd &&
			            NOT(ISBLANK('Tenancy'[Vacated Date])) &&
			            RELATED('Property'[Program]) = "Transitional Housing" &&
			            NOT('Tenancy'[Exit Outcome] = "Internal Transfer")
			        )
			    )
			VAR _HouseholdsServicedThisMonth =
			    CALCULATE(
			        COUNTROWS('Tenancy'),
			        'Property'[Program] = "Transitional Housing",
			        'Tenancy'[Tenancy Start Date] <= _MonthEnd,
			        OR(
			            ISBLANK('Tenancy'[Vacated Date]),
			            'Tenancy'[Vacated Date] >= _MonthStart
			        )
			    )
			RETURN
			    DIVIDE(_ExitsThisMonth, _HouseholdsServicedThisMonth, BLANK())
		formatString: 0.0%
		displayFolder: 09. THVM Dashboard\Exits
		lineageTag: f5242fb8-37f9-449b-b3d7-4761aa6fbe3e

	/// Displays the gap status between this tenancy and the previous one for the same tenant. Shows: 'First Tenancy' if no prior tenancy exists, 'Continuous (X days gap)' if gap is 3 days or less (part of same chain), 'New Chain (X days gap)' if gap exceeds 3 days (starts new chain). Use in row-level context with Tenancy table.
	measure 'Stay Chain Gap Check' =
			VAR TenantCtx = SELECTEDVALUE(Tenancy[Tenant Name])
			
			// Get gap days for the current tenancy row context
			VAR GapDays = SELECTEDVALUE(Tenancy[Gap Days])
			VAR PrevVacate = SELECTEDVALUE(Tenancy[Prev Vacate Date])
			
			RETURN
			SWITCH(
			    TRUE(),
			    ISBLANK(TenantCtx), BLANK(),
			    ISBLANK(PrevVacate), "First Tenancy",
			    GapDays <= 3, "Continuous (" & GapDays & " days gap)",
			    "New Chain (" & GapDays & " days gap)"
			)
		isHidden
		displayFolder: _Internal
		lineageTag: 8aa5f401-cbf1-4d72-b296-69b16d6c2485

	/// Continuous length of stay in days for the tenancy in context, measured from its Chain Start Date to the end of the selected month. A chain links consecutive tenancies where the gap between them is 3 days or less. Responds to the Date Table slicer (defaults to the current month); returns blank when a single Chain Start Date cannot be resolved in context.
	measure 'Total Length of Stay (Days)' =
			VAR _RefDate = IF(ISFILTERED('Date Table'), MAX('Date Table'[Calendar Date]), TODAY())
			VAR MonthEnd = EOMONTH(_RefDate, 0)
			VAR ChainStart = SELECTEDVALUE('Tenancy'[Chain Start Date])
			RETURN
			IF(
			    ISBLANK(ChainStart) || ISBLANK(MonthEnd),
			    BLANK(),
			    DATEDIFF(ChainStart, MonthEnd, DAY) + 1
			)
		formatString: #,0
		displayFolder: 09. THVM Dashboard\Length of Stay
		lineageTag: 7e733c4f-4968-41f1-83a1-e0de05352a13

	/// Count of active primary tenants (one per active tenancy) whose tenancy overlaps the selected period - started on/before period end and not vacated before period start - EXCLUDING cancelled tenancies (aligned with the gender and ethnicity sub-measures so the demographic completeness denominators are consistent). (Period): responds to the Date Table slicer, FY 1 Jul to 30 Jun; with no slicer counts all-time. Grain: primary-tenant records.
	measure 'Total Active Tenants (Period)' =
			VAR MinDate = MIN('Date Table'[Calendar Date])
			VAR MaxDate = MAX('Date Table'[Calendar Date])
			RETURN
			IF(
			    ISBLANK(MinDate) || ISBLANK(MaxDate),
			    COUNTROWS(FILTER(Tenant, Tenant[Is Primary Tenant] = 1 && Tenant[Tenancy Status] <> "Cancelled")),
			    CALCULATE(
			        COUNTROWS(Tenant),
			        FILTER(
			            Tenant,
			            Tenant[Tenancy Start Date] <= MaxDate &&
			            (ISBLANK(RELATED(Tenancy[Vacated Date])) || RELATED(Tenancy[Vacated Date]) >= MinDate) &&
			            Tenant[Is Primary Tenant] = 1 &&
			            Tenant[Tenancy Status] <> "Cancelled"
			        ),
			        REMOVEFILTERS('Date Table')
			    )
			)
		formatString: #,0
		displayFolder: 10. Tenant Demographics
		lineageTag: 7dbde3ab-f71a-43df-b2dc-273fe7eb251e

	/// Count of primary-tenant records classified as Maori (Ethnicity in Maori, New Zealand Maori) whose tenancy overlaps the selected period; excludes cancelled tenancies. (Period): responds to the Date Table slicer, FY 1 Jul to 30 Jun; with no slicer counts all-time. CAVEAT: currently returns BLANK - Ethnicity is 100% NULL for primary tenants (captured only on non-primary household-member rows), so the breakdown is non-functional until the source/grain is fixed.
	measure 'Tenants - Maori (Period)' =
			VAR MinDate = MIN('Date Table'[Calendar Date])
			VAR MaxDate = MAX('Date Table'[Calendar Date])
			VAR EthnicityValues = {"Maori", "New Zealand Maori"}
			RETURN
			IF(
			    ISBLANK(MinDate) || ISBLANK(MaxDate),
			    COUNTROWS(
			        FILTER(
			            Tenant,
			            Tenant[Is Primary Tenant] = 1 &&
			            Tenant[Tenancy Status] <> "Cancelled" &&
			            Tenant[Ethnicity] IN EthnicityValues
			        )
			    ),
			    CALCULATE(
			        COUNTROWS(Tenant),
			        FILTER(
			            Tenant,
			            Tenant[Tenancy Start Date] <= MaxDate &&
			            (ISBLANK(RELATED(Tenancy[Vacated Date])) || RELATED(Tenancy[Vacated Date]) >= MinDate) &&
			            Tenant[Is Primary Tenant] = 1 &&
			            Tenant[Tenancy Status] <> "Cancelled" &&
			            Tenant[Ethnicity] IN EthnicityValues
			        ),
			        REMOVEFILTERS('Date Table')
			    )
			)
		formatString: #,0
		displayFolder: 10. Tenant Demographics\Ethnicity
		lineageTag: a927f5f9-e8c1-4793-8a0e-aa23e03d3448

